<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Nöteborg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1323</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Treaty of Orekhovets · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-novgorodian-wars">Swedish–Novgorodian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oreshek-fortress">Nöteborg</a> was a peace concluded in 1323 at the fortress of Nöteborg (Orekhovets) at the source of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neva-river">Neva</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and the Novgorod Republic. It drew the first agreed border across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a>, leaving the western part with Sweden and the east with Novgorod. The line shaped the later divide between Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-noteborg.jpg" alt="Treaty of Nöteborg" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Velivieras · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:P%C3%A4hkin%C3%A4saaren_rauhan_raja_1323_-_Treaty_of_N%C3%B6teborg_1323.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
